 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+36}Ar ground state.                                       
 35CL c  1993Ma50: a 52-MeV polarized deuteron beam at 15 nA was produced from  
 35CL2c  the Karlsruhe isochronous cyclotron at the Max-Plank-Institut fur      
 35CL3c  Kernphysik. The target was 350-mbar 99.86% enriched {+36}Ar gas.       
 35CL4c  Reaction products were detected using a Si detector telescope          
 35CL5c  consisting of a 250-|mm |DE-strip detector and a 1.5 -mm               
 35CL6c  surface-barrier E detector with FWHM=130 keV. Measured angular         
 35CL7c  distributions of cross sections |s(E({+3}He),|q) and angular           
 35CL8c  distributions of analyzing powers iT{-11}(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced       
 35CL9c  levels, J, |p, L-transfers, and spectroscopic factors from DWBA        
 35CLAc  analysis of |s(E({+3}He),|q) and iT{-11}(E({+3}He),|q).                
 35CL c  1993Ma50 states that spectroscopic factors were obtained by fitting the
 35CL2c  forward-angle maxima. The agreement with the analyzing powers is only  
 35CL3c  qualitative. The determination of spins and parities of final states is
 35CL4c  mainly based on a comparison with measured angular distributions       
 35CL5c  leading to final states with known spins. The comparison with DWBA     
 35CL6c  predictions serves as additional check. The data were taken only in a  
 35CL7c  relatively small angle interval. This is sufficient for the spin       
 35CL8c  determination but not favorable for the measurement of spectroscopic   
 35CL9c  factors.                                                               
 35CL cL $Spectroscopic factor C{+2}S=|s(|q){-exp}/|s(|q){-DWBA}/N, where N=2.95
